d2d1: Present DC-direct HwndRenderTargets at EndDraw only, not on Flush.

Lab After Effects 2026 (clean-room AE2026, 11.10-146 to 149): with the Composition panel maximized (backtick), a black
strip spans the full width under the panel's tab row, where the restored panel shows its "Comp 1" button. It stays
until something else repaints the panel.

After Effects paints the panel in one BeginDraw..EndDraw and calls ID2D1DeviceContext::Flush twice in the middle. The
navigator row (a full-width 3834x70 fill, the "Comp 1" button, its text, the border line) is drawn after the first
Flush. Flush calls the present hook, as in upstream Wine. Under DC-direct (NEUTRON_D2D_DCDIRECT=1: After Effects,
Premiere, Media Encoder, Audition) that present blitted the drawn region back into the window and released the frame
DC taken at BeginDraw, so the second Flush and EndDraw had no DC and blitted nothing. Whatever the app drew after its
first Flush reached the window only on the panel's next paint, from the retained bitmap. After a resize the bitmap is
new, so the row stayed black (all zeros), and After Effects asks for no further paint.

In the D2D API, Flush executes the pending commands and an HwndRenderTarget presents in EndDraw (documented behavior,
not measured on Windows). Now a Flush does not present a DC-direct HwndRenderTarget: EndDraw blits the region drawn
since BeginDraw (the union already accumulates from BeginDraw) and releases the frame DC.

harnesses/d2d-flush-present.c (child window, HwndRenderTarget with RETAIN_CONTENTS | IMMEDIATELY: BeginDraw, top half
red, Flush, bottom half blue, Flush, EndDraw, then GetDC readback), NEUTRON_D2D_DCDIRECT=1: 149 leaves the bottom half
black (FAIL); with this patch both halves show (PASS); kill switch off: FAIL. Without Flush, or without DC-direct: PASS
either way.
Lab After Effects 2026 (149 + this d2d1): the maximized panel shows its row (band mean 30,30,30 and the "Comp 1"
button), 2 of 2 maximizes; 149: black (0,0,0) every time. A lab-only op trace showed the row's draws are identical in
the first frame after the resize and in a forced repaint; only their delivery differed.
Lab Premiere 2026 makes no Flush calls (0 in a session with every d2d FIXME logged), so its drawing is unchanged; four
maximized panels render normally. Lab Media Encoder 2026 does (140 at startup): with the patch and with the kill switch
off its window is pixel-identical in two matched states (Queue panel maximized; preset list expanded).
Kill switch NEUTRON_D2D_FLUSH_HOLD=0.

--- a/dlls/d2d1/d2d1_private.h
+++ b/dlls/d2d1/d2d1_private.h
@@ -107,6 +107,10 @@
  * into hdc at the same position. Returns FALSE if unavailable (caller falls back to GetDC). */
 BOOL neutron_dc_readback_blit(ID2D1RenderTarget *rt, HDC hdc, const RECT *rect);
 void neutron_dc_readback_release(ID2D1RenderTarget *rt);
+
+/* NEUTRON D2D FLUSH-HOLD: TRUE while ID2D1DeviceContext::Flush is calling the present hook. Defined in
+ * device.c. */
+BOOL neutron_dr_in_flush(ID2D1RenderTarget *rt);
 void neutron_dr_get_draw_stats(ID2D1RenderTarget *rt, unsigned *prims, unsigned *draws,
         LONGLONG *in_d2d, LONGLONG *worst_prim);
 
@@ -236,6 +240,22 @@
     return v;
 }
 
+/* NEUTRON D2D FLUSH-HOLD (default ON, env NEUTRON_D2D_FLUSH_HOLD=0 restores presenting on Flush): a DC-direct
+ * HwndRenderTarget presents at EndDraw only, as on Windows, where Flush executes the pending commands and an
+ * HwndRenderTarget presents in EndDraw. Presenting on Flush released the frame DC, so everything the app drew
+ * after its first Flush never reached the window: After Effects draws a maximized panel's navigator row after
+ * two mid-frame Flushes, and the row stayed black (harnesses/d2d-flush-present.c). */
+static inline BOOL neutron_flush_hold(void)
+{
+    static int v = -1;
+    if (v < 0)
+    {
+        char buf[8];
+        v = (GetEnvironmentVariableA("NEUTRON_D2D_FLUSH_HOLD", buf, sizeof(buf)) && buf[0] == '0') ? 0 : 1;
+    }
+    return v;
+}
+
 static inline BOOL neutron_maskrects(void)
 {
     static int v = -1;
@@ -776,6 +796,7 @@
     unsigned nb_ops;
     unsigned neutron_draw_ops;   /* NEUTRON: always-on drawing-call count since BeginDraw */
     unsigned neutron_clear_first; /* NEUTRON: this frame's first op was a Clear */
+    BOOL neutron_in_flush;        /* NEUTRON FLUSH-HOLD: Flush is calling the present hook */
     /* NEUTRON op-trace: did the app CLEAR this frame, and over what clip? A frame that
      * clears the panel and then draws almost nothing is the app wiping its own content --
      * not us erasing it. Reset with the unions at BeginDraw. */
--- a/dlls/d2d1/device.c
+++ b/dlls/d2d1/device.c
@@ -1255,6 +1255,12 @@
     }
 }
 
+/* NEUTRON FLUSH-HOLD: is this present coming from Flush rather than EndDraw? */
+BOOL neutron_dr_in_flush(ID2D1RenderTarget *rt)
+{
+    return impl_from_ID2D1DeviceContext((ID2D1DeviceContext6 *)rt)->neutron_in_flush;
+}
+
 /* NEUTRON op-trace: this frame's op count, clear count and the clear's bounds. */
 void neutron_dr_get_frame_stats(ID2D1RenderTarget *rt, unsigned *ops, unsigned *clears, RECT *clear_rect)
 {
@@ -3541,7 +3547,11 @@
     d2d_device_context_release_state(context);
 
     if (context->ops && context->ops->device_context_present)
+    {
+        context->neutron_in_flush = TRUE;
         context->ops->device_context_present(context->outer_unknown);
+        context->neutron_in_flush = FALSE;
+    }
 
     return S_OK;
 }
--- a/dlls/d2d1/hwnd_render_target.c
+++ b/dlls/d2d1/hwnd_render_target.c
@@ -301,6 +301,11 @@
     {
         RECT u = {0}; BOOL uv = FALSE;
 
+        /* NEUTRON FLUSH-HOLD: a Flush inside BeginDraw..EndDraw does not present. EndDraw blits the
+         * union drawn since BeginDraw, and releases the frame DC taken there. */
+        if (neutron_flush_hold() && neutron_dr_in_flush(render_target->dxgi_target))
+            return S_OK;
+
         /* Present-rate probe: a window presenting at hundreds/s is spinning, not drawing. */
         if (!render_target->pres_tick0)
             render_target->pres_tick0 = GetTickCount() | 1;
